### Orders: the 120 sample orders and the orders OrderPilot stores itself.
### Read-only today: there is no write route until P-49. Each row says its source
### (sample or stored). A stored order has no workflow status, only a capture
### state (draft, submitted or void), which is not the order's status.
### Sign in first (see auth.http): REST Client keeps the cookies.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Sign in as Support, who sees amounts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "SUPPORT" }

### Orders, a page at a time, newest first. Amounts are masked by role.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?page=1&pageSize=25

### Sort by orderNo, customerNo, orderDate, shipmentDate, amount or captureState.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?sort=amount&direction=desc
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?sort=shipmentDate&direction=asc

### Search covers the order number, the customer number and the customer's PO number.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?search=SO-00

### One customer, by Navision number.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?customerNo=C-0001

### Capture state applies to stored orders only: a sample has none.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?captureState=draft
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?source=stored

### Order date and amount ranges.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?orderDateFrom=2026-10-01&orderDateTo=2026-10-31
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?amountFrom=1000&amountTo=5000

### Orders waiting on stock. Each says by how much it is short: the list only
### shows the gap, and nothing is ordered for it. The value is `waiting`, never `true`.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?stock=waiting

### One order, with its lines and what falls short of stock.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-0001

### An unknown number answers the 404 envelope.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-20990101-0001

### A bad query answers the 400 envelope with the fields that failed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?pageSize=500&stock=true

### Sign in as WAREHOUSE and the same requests answer amount, unitPrice and
### lineAmount as masked: true, value: null, reason "price". Sorting by amount
### then gives the default order, and an amount range is ignored.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "WAREHOUSE" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-0001

### SYSTEM_ADMIN holds no orders.read: 403, and the refusal is audited.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "SYSTEM_ADMIN" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
